data.content:
All three pieces of your code are affected by EF Core 10 breaking changes. Here's what breaks and how to fix each:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — expression tree no longer compiles

The parameter changed from `Expression<Func<...>>` to `Func<...>`. Your manual expression tree building won't compile. Replace with a simple lambda:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

### 2. Complex types — column name changes (two issues)

**a) Same-named properties are now uniquified.** If `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` previously shared one `Street` column, EF 10 will generate `Street` and `Street1`. To keep them shared, pin the name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});
```

**b) Nested complex types now use full path.** `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` was previously column `BillingAddress_City`; it's now `Payment_BillingAddress_City`. To keep the old name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

> ⚠️ Both changes affect migrations — expect a generated migration that renames columns. Either pin names as above, or apply the migration to adopt the new defaults.

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method now requires an additional `string logCommandText` parameter (for redacted SQL logging). Add it:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText (redacted) for logging instead of command.CommandText
    }
}
```

Update **all** methods on the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) the same way.
